      {
        "id": 57799,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-11T17:25:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The other way it was viewed is:</p><p>If a card effect affects the hero, it is prevented by isolation.</p><p>If a card effect affects a non-hero card it is fine. &nbsp;</p><p>Examples:</p><p>If Wraith shoots badguy with stun bolts and badguy deals damage to isolated hero, that -1 to damage dealt is valid.</p><p>If Wraith has Smoke Grenades out and the Isolated Hero is the lowest HP hero, the isolated hero gains no benefit from Smoke Bombs.</p><p>if Isolated Hero would take 5 damage and Non-Isolated Tempest has shielding winds the damage is not reduced, since Shielding Winds effect cannot help the hero.</p><p>One of the points of contention was By Any Means, which increases damage dealt to a villain, and therefore in this interpretation is valid, since the effect is not on the hero.</p>",
        "post_number": 129,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:33:12.503Z",
