      {
        "id": 57803,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-11T17:44:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes, I think Foote and I would even agree that destroying an ongoing would be legit.(although if it was a jinx on the isolated player we might disagree)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The only reason I disagree with destroying a jinx is because kismet and miss info don't fight together in a legal game format haha.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ongoing destruction (if it doesn't belong to the isolated hero or vice versa) &nbsp;is fine.&nbsp;</p>",
